From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:52:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 126/142] compiler: a class helper's alias procsym is refilled,
 not dereferenced, when its symtable resolves again

Re-resolving the symbol tables loaded from a ppu when a used unit is recompiled (a7b0e8a265)
runs the interface dereference again. A class helper's alias procsym (CH$<name>,
create_class_helper_for_procdef) is made when the helper's implementation is dereferenced
and is not stored, so it has no dereference data, and tprocsym.deref stopped with internal
error 200611031. Such an alias now only clears its procdef list; the helper's derefimpl fills
it again.

Test: tests/tppu/reloadhelper (TTestRecompile.TestReloadClassHelper), a loaded unit's class
helper after control's new CRC recompiles base.
---
 compiler/symsym.pas                           | 11 +++++++-
 tests/tppu/reloadhelper/ppus/.gitignore       |  1 +
 tests/tppu/reloadhelper/reloadhelper_base.pas | 16 +++++++++++
 .../tppu/reloadhelper/reloadhelper_child.pas  | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 tests/tppu/reloadhelper/reloadhelper_prg.pas  | 15 ++++++++++
 .../src1/reloadhelper_control.pas             | 22 +++++++++++++++
 .../src2/reloadhelper_control.pas             | 22 +++++++++++++++
 tests/tppu/tcrecompile.pas                    | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 8 files changed, 142 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/tppu/reloadhelper/ppus/.gitignore
 create mode 100644 tests/tppu/reloadhelper/reloadhelper_base.pas
 create mode 100644 tests/tppu/reloadhelper/reloadhelper_child.pas
 create mode 100644 tests/tppu/reloadhelper/reloadhelper_prg.pas
 create mode 100644 tests/tppu/reloadhelper/src1/reloadhelper_control.pas
 create mode 100644 tests/tppu/reloadhelper/src2/reloadhelper_control.pas

diff --git a/compiler/symsym.pas b/compiler/symsym.pas
index b46cb69d..4de3dc15 100644
--- a/compiler/symsym.pas
+++ b/compiler/symsym.pas
@@ -1157,7 +1157,16 @@ implementation
         { Clear all procdefs }
         ProcdefList.Clear;
         if not assigned(FProcdefDerefList) then
-          internalerror(200611031);
+          begin
+            { a class helper's alias (create_class_helper_for_procdef) is made
+              when the helper's implementation is dereferenced and is not
+              stored, so it has no dereference data: when a recompiled unit
+              makes its symtable resolve again, the helper's derefimpl fills
+              it again }
+            if copy(name,1,length(class_helper_prefix))=class_helper_prefix then
+              exit;
+            internalerror(200611031);
+          end;
         ProcdefList.capacity:=FProcdefDerefList.count;
         for i:=0 to FProcdefDerefList.Count-1 do
           begin
